# GOLDEN RA RB DISJOINT
# GOLDEN-NOSOLVER RA RB POSSIBLY
# GROUND-TRUTH: presence itself carries the disjointness, and it cannot be
#   wrong: an event either has a value for a quantity or it does not.
#   RA requires `btag(jets[0])` to have a value (any comparison over it does).
#   RB's reject HOLDS only when it does not, because a present btag is either
#   0 or 1 and `>= 0` then fails the reject. So the pair is disjoint on
#   DEFINEDNESS alone, with the tag values irrelevant.
#
#   The solver-less pin records a DEVIATION from SPEC_PRESENCE_MODEL s7(a),
#   which expected this class on the interval fast path ("one region requires
#   the quantity present, the other requires it absent" as two bounds on one
#   presence quantity). That shape is unreachable: ADL has no way to SELECT
#   absence, so `p < 1` only ever arrives as one disjunct of a negated leaf,
#   and the interval spine skips disjunctions by construction. RB's encoding
#   is `p < 1 or btag < 0`, and killing the second disjunct needs TAG - i.e.
#   the solver. Capping at POSSIBLY without one is the correct fail-closed
#   behaviour, not a regression.

object jets
  take Jet
  select pt > 30

region RA
  select size(jets) >= 1
  select BTag(jets[0]) >= 0

region RB
  select size(jets) >= 1
  reject BTag(jets[0]) >= 0
